{"skill":{"slug":"agent-autopilot","displayName":"Agent Autopilot"},"version":{"version":"1.4.1","createdAt":1771763437370,"changelog":"缩短description，修复ClawHub页面渲染溢出问题","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":16117,"sha256":"8f3639890b4f6c5cc0aaf22b1d8e935626d24e67e607e52bf73eb8f2ade109a2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/example-setup.md","size":6903,"sha256":"989c32aa7297b655e627d143fadc08e203d6a2f4572d884fc67b182339961a8b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/init.sh","size":2419,"sha256":"5f2a506686c8b43800e00fbd3dc8365261685c38112b4475e997e3e682ed5f88","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2616,"sha256":"360f2a3a4b96b5adc7fb22108bbfa75ae677b8521460195311c1e529cead6226","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789077865507,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a9475d932046e16647889fdddea51f96eb31cc140f9ed0e185666501d21e2634","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a9475d932046e16647889fdddea51f96eb31cc140f9ed0e185666501d21e2634","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: agent-autopilot\nVersion: 1.4.1\n\nThe skill bundle instructs the AI agent to execute shell commands, specifically `bash {todoBaseDir}/scripts/todo.sh ...`. While this is necessary for its stated purpose of task management, the template `bash {todoBaseDir}/scripts/todo.sh entry create \"...\" --group=\"{项目名}\"` in `SKILL.md` and `HEARTBEAT.md` presents a shell injection vulnerability. If the AI agent, when autonomously creating new tasks, generates a `{项目名}` value from untrusted input or its own analysis that contains shell metacharacters, this could lead to arbitrary command execution. This is a significant risk, even if not intentionally malicious by the skill developer. The skill also grants the agent broad file system and `git` access, which, while necessary for its function, increases the attack surface if the agent is compromised or misdirected.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779166101635},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":53,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789077865507},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is not overtly malicious, but it should be reviewed carefully because it creates an unbounded autonomous heartbeat loop and persistent memory rewriting.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The workflow can repeatedly exercise whatever shell, file, API, or messaging authority the hosting agent already has, while the artifact provides only limited scoping guidance.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The init script is simple and local: it creates workspace directories, copies the todo-management skill from an existing local/global install if present, and creates report-state.json. It does not fetch remote code, but it modifies the user-supplied workspace without a confirmation gate.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The HEARTBEAT.md template suppresses the normal idle response, tells the agent not to ask a supervisor what to do, and lacks clear per-action approval, maximum iteration, or stop boundaries.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill instructs users to write operational rules into HEARTBEAT.md and MEMORY.md, update report-state.json, append daily logs, and periodically rewrite MEMORY.md including removing information considered outdated.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The self-driving task execution, progress reporting, and memory consolidation match the stated purpose, but the artifact directs the agent to keep working on every heartbeat, create new tasks when prior tasks are done, and continue until a broad goal is reached.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only in an isolated workspace with limited tool permissions. Before enabling heartbeat automation, edit the templates to require explicit approval for new tasks, external APIs, commits, network use, destructive or account-impacting actions, and any MEMORY.md rewrite; keep version history for memory files and avoid attaching real trading, financial, or production credentials until those controls exist.","findings":"[T01] expected: Heartbeat-driven work is central to the skill, but the artifact-backed wording makes it materially under-scoped by requiring work on every heartbeat and autonomous task creation without clear stop limits.\n[T02] expected: Long-term memory consolidation is disclosed and purpose-aligned, but recurring MEMORY.md rewriting and cleanup without review is a real persistence and control concern.\n[SQP-2] expected: Persistent writes to todo state, memory logs, MEMORY.md, and report-state.json are expected for this workflow, but several are automatic and lack explicit review, dry-run, rollback, or bounded activation controls.\n[SQP-3] expected: The Chinese-language instructions and Chinese commit-message example are visible in the artifact and are mainly a usability/localization issue, not a security reason for the Review verdict.\n[SDI-1] expected: The cryptocurrency quantitative-strategy material appears to be an example of a project this workflow might manage; it broadens the apparent use case but does not by itself show hidden trading execution or credential use.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789077865507}}}}}